@startuml Authentication Flow - OAuth 2.0 with Google
autonumber

title Authentication Flow - Google OAuth 2.0

actor "User" as user
participant "Frontend" as frontend
participant "NGINX" as nginx
participant "API Gateway" as gateway
participant "Google\nOAuth" as google

user -> frontend: Click "Login with Google"
activate frontend

frontend -> nginx: Redirect to\n/api/auth/google
activate nginx

nginx -> gateway: Forward auth request
activate gateway

gateway -> google: Redirect to Google OAuth\n(ClientId, Scope, RedirectUri)
activate google

google --> user: Show Google login page
user -> google: Enter credentials\nand authorize

google -> gateway: Callback with\nAuthorization Code
deactivate google

gateway -> google: Exchange code for\nAccess Token & ID Token
activate google
google --> gateway: Access Token & ID Token
deactivate google

gateway -> gateway: Validate ID Token\n(Signature, Issuer, Audience)

gateway -> gateway: Extract user claims\n(email, name, picture)

gateway -> gateway: Check if email in\nAdminEmails list

gateway -> gateway: Create authentication cookie\n(Encrypted, HttpOnly, SameSite)

gateway --> nginx: Set-Cookie header\nRedirect to /
deactivate gateway

nginx --> frontend: 302 Redirect with cookie
deactivate nginx

frontend -> nginx: GET / (with cookie)
activate nginx

nginx -> gateway: Forward request with cookie
activate gateway

gateway -> gateway: Validate cookie
gateway -> gateway: Restore user session

gateway --> nginx: 200 OK with user info
deactivate gateway

nginx --> frontend: 200 OK
deactivate nginx

frontend --> user: Show authenticated UI
deactivate frontend

note right of gateway
  Subsequent API requests include
  the authentication cookie.
  
  JWT Bearer tokens are also
  supported for API clients.
end note

@enduml
